    {
      "id": "ML-C97-bhangi",
      "sequence": 3450,
      "title": "ഭംഗി (bhaṅgi) — beauty",
      "headword": "ഭംഗി",
      "romanization": "bhaṅgi",
      "gloss": "beauty — the thing itself, and a word that welds onto ആണ് a different way",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:407543d53bba55c1",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say this is beautiful. Then say child — you have had that word a long time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഭംഗി — bhaṅgi — beauty, the thing itself rather than the quality."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് ഭംഗിയാണ്. — itŭ bhaṅgiyāṇŭ — \"This is beauty.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This one does not end in ം, and it shows. Read the two welds side by side:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "സുന്ദരം (sundaraṁ) becomes സുന്ദരമാണ്, a മ appears.",
                "ഭംഗി (bhaṅgi) becomes ഭംഗിയാണ്, a യ appears."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have seen the second one before, on a word you learned long ago: ഇത് എന്റെ കുട്ടിയാണ് — this is my child."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neither word loses anything. A letter arrives to carry the vowel of ആണ്, and which letter arrives depends on how the word ended. That is the whole difference."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "bhaṅgi, then bhaṅgiyāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *bhaṅgi*, then *bhaṅgiyāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "sundaraṁ, then sundaramāṇŭ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *sundaraṁ*, then *sundaramāṇŭ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at the two joined forms, and name the letter that differs",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at the two joined forms, and name the letter that differs]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is beauty? (ഭംഗി (bhaṅgi).) Which letter appears when ആണ് follows it? (യ.) And after a word ending in ം? (മ.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ML-C97-alla-sundaram",
      "sequence": 3460,
      "title": "ഇത് സുന്ദരം അല്ല (itŭ sundaraṁ alla) — this is not beautiful",
      "headword": "ഇത് സുന്ദരം അല്ല",
      "romanization": "itŭ sundaraṁ alla",
      "gloss": "this is not beautiful — the far end of the same line, built with the denial word you already have",
      "script": "malayalam",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:a316206014b28b7f",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say this is beautiful. Then say the word that denies being what you were called."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the denial stands apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇത് സുന്ദരം അല്ല. — itŭ sundaraṁ alla — \"This is not beautiful.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Look at what did not happen. അല്ല did not weld onto the word in front of it, the way ആണ് did. It stands on its own, after the thing being denied — exactly as you first met it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 2,
              "utterances": [
                "ഞാൻ അധ്യാപകൻ അല്ല, I am not a teacher.",
                "ഇത് സുന്ദരം അല്ല (itŭ sundaraṁ alla), this is not beautiful."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Same shape, different subject. The word being denied sits in the middle, unchanged and unwelded, and സുന്ദരം (sundaraṁ) keeps its ം because nothing attached to it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Both ends of the same line, from one new word and one you already had."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is how the far end of most qualities will arrive for a while: not by a second word, but by denying the first one. It is what a learner can actually use early, and it is what a Malayalam speaker often says anyway."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
